From a7eee72b2df2784f8e58c7d1bdb985b5611049b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ran shalit <rshalit@habana.ai>
Date: Mon, 26 Jun 2023 10:41:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [SW-149942] efuse: add init as part of general flow

efuse init was recently removed, as part of a patch
which removes tpm enable:
[SW-142278] h6: tpm: remove tpm_en efuse bit check

efuse init was done in code in the first attempt to read
efuse, hence - since no one reads anything from efuse
(as part of the above patch), there is no init and any other
later project (preboot, mgmt etc) fails in efuse read.

This patch fix this issue by forcing efuse init as part
of general initialization in main.

Change-Id: Id788b858a4f00a05430cced4b1cda560cfec92ef
Signed-off-by: ran shalit <rshalit@habana.ai>
---

diff --git a/app/preboot/preboot.c b/app/preboot/preboot.c
index b087b1a..1c6d59c 100644
--- a/app/preboot/preboot.c
+++ b/app/preboot/preboot.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <boot_info.h>
 #include <hl_boot_desc.h>
 #include <crc32.h>
+#include <efuse.h>
 #include <rma_if.h>	/* required for nvme data */
 #include <hl_nvme_mi_data.h>
 #include <hl_i2c_indirect_protocol.h>
@@ -479,6 +480,7 @@
 	hl_dev_pll_init();
 
 	hl_uart_init();
+	preboot_fuse_init();
 
 	preboot_close_strap_eeprom_write();
 
